    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0394" n="1024" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg1024"/>

                <head>No. 417.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General <persName corresp="#p_DES1"
                            type="from">Sickles</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="to">Fish</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                                States Legation in Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 8, 1873</date>.
                        (Received August 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 686.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward a translation
                    of a communication from a person identified with the insurgent movement in
                    Valencia, addressed to the United States consul. Also, translation of a reply
                    made on behalf of all the consuls by Mr. <persName>Cialdini</persName>, the
                    Italian vice-consul.</p>
                <p>The papers having been transmitted to me by Mr. <persName>Loewenstein</persName>,
                    in charge of the United States consulate at Valencia, accompanied by a report of
                    his proceedings, a copy of which is inclosed, I sent him certain instructions,
                    winch will be found in Appendix C.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_DES1">D. E. SICKLES</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>






